mothers music is highly strong extremely  loud or soft full of strong emotions  fantastic contrasts it is as he lived in  a state of continuous excitement it is  highly unusual for anyone to compose  music which transmits this level of  agitation the average genius allow me to  say average genius even if he is nervous  wide overexcited in real life like  Beethoven for example finds a way to  control language and form indeed  mother's work is masterful and perfect  on the one hand there are no mistakes  where harmony counterpoint or any other  compositional skill are concerned and  this high degree of perfection clearly  shows us a genius at work on the other  hand however no attempt is made here to  tame the occasional shapeless flow of  weird and unpredictable ideas mal are  composed for following his inspiration  as if the music were dictated to him he  turned his state of excitement and his  arsenal of memories into music  translating this intensity and this vast  collection of fragmented impressions  into a musical language so that it can  be shared with others is the essence of  Mahler's art I use the word translate  following Spinoza's thoughts in his  tractor to stay logical politicals where  he mentions that  Hebrew world Navi means both translator  and profit was Mallory prophet he was  certainly a seer who could sense future  events mother died in 1911 in the den  still peaceful Habsburg Empire he would  never get to read Spengler's in taganga  Ivan Landess which was published seven  years later he didn't live to see the  horrors of the two world wars he didn't  live to experience the Holocaust yet one  cannot escape the feeling that in his  music we hear a foreboding a vision of  these terrible future events the funeral  marches in the second fifth and sixth  symphonies the frequent appearance of  military fanfares  the young soldier who is mesmerised by  the gallows the heartbreakingly hopeless  march in the sleet from the air these  seem like musical descriptions of later  tragedies we hear soldiers marching in  heavy boots and we hear the pain of the  hunted tortured victims mothers music is  an uninhibited outpouring of of his own  psyche but malar was no over sentimental  adolescent who wanted to share his  misery with the world he could see  terrible things coming living in Carroll  Lugar's  Vienna with his fine perceptive instinct  he must have felt the roots of tensions  that led to the assassination in  Sarajevo and to the emergence of Hitler  as Leonard Bernstein observed in his  essay about Mahler and I quote from  birth time the music is almost cruel in  his revelations it is like a camera that  has caught Western society in the moment  of its incipient  decay only after we have experienced all  this through the smoking ovens of  Auschwitz the frenetically bombed  jungles of Vietnam and here follows  Bernstein's long long list of tragic and  inhuman events of the 20th century only  after all this he continues can we  finally listen to Mahler's music and  understand that it foretold all there is  nothing mystical about this there were  others who sensed the end of the world  the Letson targeter mensch height as  Karl Kraus expressed it a few years  later but the greatest prophet in  fantasy occur Vienna who composed the  funeral music for the 20th century more  convincingly than anybody else was  Gustav Mahler
 

